Description: Persistent terminal sessions for the meshTerm iOS app, plus the mtctl CLI.
 meshtermd is a per-user daemon that hosts QUIC/Roam terminal sessions which
 survive disconnects and roaming; mtctl is the laptop CLI that attaches to a
 remote daemon over SSH+QUIC. Runs as a systemd --user service (one per login
 user) — it spawns shells as you, so it is never a system-wide daemon.

